{"id":"s1.4.7","slug":"converting-fractions-to-decimals-40-80","title":"Converting a/40 and b/80, etc... to Decimals","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">Converting fractions with denominators like 40 or 80 can be simplified by breaking down the process.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">For a fraction $\\frac{a}{40}$, treat it as $\\frac{a/4}{10}$. First, divide the numerator by 4, then shift the decimal point one place to the left.</p><p>Example: $\\frac{43}{40} = 1 + \\frac{3}{40}$. For the fractional part, calculate $3 \\div 4 = 0.75$. Shift the decimal: 0.075. So, $\\frac{43}{40} = 1.075$.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">Similarly, for $\\frac{b}{80}$, treat it as $\\frac{b/8}{10}$. Divide the numerator by 8, then shift the decimal.</p><p>Example: $\\frac{27}{80}$. Calculate $27 \\div 8 = 3.375$. Shift the decimal: 0.3375.</p>","summary":"Converting fractions with denominators like 40 or 80 can be simplified by breaking down the process.","generation_guideline":"Ask to convert a fraction with a denominator of 40 or 80 to a decimal.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"Convert $\\frac{1}{40}$ to a percent.","answer":"2.5%","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","percent","repeating-decimals","conversions"]},{"id":2,"text":"Convert $\\frac{3}{40}$ to a percent.","answer":"7.5%","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","percent","repeating-decimals","conversions"]},{"id":3,"text":"Convert $\\frac{7}{40}$ to a percent.","answer":"17.5%","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","percent","repeating-decimals","conversions"]},{"id":4,"text":"Convert $\\frac{21}{40}$ to a percent.","answer":"52.5%","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","percent","repeating-decimals","conversions"]},{"id":5,"text":"Convert $\\frac{43}{40}$ to a decimal.","answer":"1.075","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","repeating-decimals","conversions"]},{"id":6,"text":"Convert $\\frac{3}{(2^3)(5^1)}$ to a decimal.","answer":".075","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","repeating-decimals","conversions"]},{"id":7,"text":"Convert .0125 to a percent (fraction 